 "pages": [
  {
   "n": 1,
   "title": "Before the First Crown",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_01.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 399370,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_01.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 283386,
   "duration": 33.01,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 10.18,
     "text": "Before Veyr had a name… before any crown was forged, or any king was laid in stone… something slept beneath the mountain."
    },
    {
     "t0": 10.93,
     "t1": 12.36,
     "text": "And it remembered."
    },
    {
     "t0": 13.11,
     "t1": 22.16,
     "text": "It kept the shape of stone. The hollow of every chamber. The weight of everything that came near it — and it let nothing go."
    },
    {
     "t0": 22.91,
     "t1": 29.49,
     "text": "Centuries later, the founders of House Vaelor broke through into the dark… and found it waiting."
    },
    {
     "t0": 30.59,
     "t1": 32.2,
     "text": "They called it the Crownheart."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 2,
   "title": "The Blood That Opened Stone",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_02.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 423630,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_02.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 311219,
   "duration": 34.61,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 7.44,
     "text": "The first rulers did not understand what they had found. They learned only this… it answered to blood."
    },
    {
     "t0": 8.19,
     "t1": 15.96,
     "text": "So they gave it theirs. Before the ancient ring, the first king opened his palm… and the stone drank."
    },
    {
     "t0": 16.71,
     "t1": 24.91,
     "text": "Doors that were never built for human hands swung open. Hidden chambers breathed again. Preserved memories obeyed."
    },
    {
     "t0": 25.66,
     "t1": 30.01,
     "text": "And a promise became a belief… and the belief became law."
    },
    {
     "t0": 31.11,
     "t1": 33.87,
     "text": "The castle remembers its rightful king."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 3,
   "title": "A Kingdom Built on Memory",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_03.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 477086,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_03.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 249734,
   "duration": 27.71,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 9.85,
     "text": "Caer Veyr rose above the Crownheart. Walls became towers. Towers became halls. And generations passed beneath its banners."
    },
    {
     "t0": 10.6,
     "t1": 17.09,
     "text": "Every coronation deepened the binding. Every royal rite drew the castle closer to the blood."
    },
    {
     "t0": 17.84,
     "t1": 21.29,
     "text": "House Vaelor believed it owned the Crownheart's memory…"
    },
    {
     "t0": 22.39,
     "t1": 26.98,
     "text": "It never understood… that the Crownheart was learning House Vaelor."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 4,
   "title": "The Last Days of Veyr",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_04.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 380184,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_04.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 284898,
   "duration": 31.81,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 8.65,
     "text": "Under King Aldren Vaelor, a long war came home at last. The fires of the siege burned from one horizon to the other."
    },
    {
     "t0": 9.4,
     "t1": 14.9,
     "text": "Behind the gates, the people of Veyr crowded into the halls… and waited for the end."
    },
    {
     "t0": 15.65,
     "t1": 22.81,
     "text": "But the king did not wait. By candlelight, deep in the royal archives, he searched the records of his fathers…"
    },
    {
     "t0": 23.91,
     "t1": 31.08,
     "text": "and he found a possibility. The whole of Caer Veyr… held forever, at one chosen moment."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 5,
   "title": "The Price of Forever",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_05.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 388516,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_05.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 289487,
   "duration": 31.21,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 9.03,
     "text": "But the Crownheart could not hold so much without living resonance. It needed lives, bound into its memory… thousands of them."
    },
    {
     "t0": 9.78,
     "t1": 14.52,
     "text": "Aldren looked upon the people sheltering inside his walls… and he chose them."
    },
    {
     "t0": 15.27,
     "t1": 20.65,
     "text": "To him, losing the kingdom was a greater crime than sacrificing those who lived in it."
    },
    {
     "t0": 21.4,
     "t1": 28.01,
     "text": "The deepest chambers were sealed. Guards turned to face inward. Servants vanished in the night…"
    },
    {
     "t0": 29.11,
     "t1": 30.44,
     "text": "and the work began."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 6,
   "title": "A House Divided",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_06.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 398498,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_06.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 323286,
   "duration": 36.01,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 4.2,
     "text": "Some at court learned what the king intended… and tried to stop him."
    },
    {
     "t0": 4.95,
     "t1": 12.48,
     "text": "And Caer Veyr turned against itself — soldiers of Veyr cutting down soldiers of Veyr, beneath the same banners."
    },
    {
     "t0": 13.23,
     "t1": 22.16,
     "text": "In the chaos, a child was taken from the castle. Royal blood, never acknowledged… never marked… never bound by the rites."
    },
    {
     "t0": 22.91,
     "t1": 28.38,
     "text": "A servants' door. A hand in the dark. The moon over the walls."
    },
    {
     "t0": 29.48,
     "t1": 35.23,
     "text": "That forgotten branch of House Vaelor would endure… long after the ruin."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 7,
   "title": "The Sundering",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_07.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 442048,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_07.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 328206,
   "duration": 36.61,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 6.03,
     "text": "At the height of the siege, Aldren descended to the Crownheart and began the ritual."
    },
    {
     "t0": 6.78,
     "t1": 11.59,
     "text": "The bells of Caer Veyr rang out… and the ritual was interrupted."
    },
    {
     "t0": 12.34,
     "t1": 20.28,
     "text": "The Crownheart failed to hold one moment. The ancient ring broke apart, and its memory tore in two —"
    },
    {
     "t0": 21.03,
     "t1": 27.81,
     "text": "the castle as it stood before the catastrophe… and the ruin it would become, generations later."
    },
    {
     "t0": 28.56,
     "t1": 32.96,
     "text": "Two remembered states, locked in the same stone."
    },
    {
     "t0": 34.06,
     "t1": 35.82,
     "text": "This was the Sundering."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 8,
   "title": "Those Who Could Not Leave",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_08.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 414320,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_08.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 323408,
   "duration": 35.41,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 8.2,
     "text": "Generations passed. The road to Caer Veyr vanished beneath the forest, and ordinary life abandoned it."
    },
    {
     "t0": 8.95,
     "t1": 16.15,
     "text": "But not everything left. Thousands of human imprints remained within the Crownheart… the Echoes."
    },
    {
     "t0": 16.9,
     "t1": 19.34,
     "text": "Some still remember who they were."
    },
    {
     "t0": 20.09,
     "t1": 27.61,
     "text": "Others keep watch at doors that no longer matter… repeating an order, long after its meaning died."
    },
    {
     "t0": 28.71,
     "t1": 34.62,
     "text": "And sometimes, in windows that fell centuries ago… a torch is burning."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 9,
   "title": "The Uncrowned",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_09.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 421656,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_09.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 315927,
   "duration": 34.31,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 13.14,
     "text": "The child who escaped did not die. Her line went on, far from Veyr — a worn crest, a half-forgotten name, a warning about a castle no one should enter."
    },
    {
     "t0": 13.89,
     "t1": 19.08,
     "text": "And from that unbound line came a woman… with a claim to the ruin."
    },
    {
     "t0": 19.83,
     "t1": 27.18,
     "text": "Vaelor blood, without the completed binding. Connected to the castle… yet not imprisoned by it."
    },
    {
     "t0": 27.93,
     "t1": 30.99,
     "text": "She came to reclaim a stolen inheritance."
    },
    {
     "t0": 32.09,
     "t1": 33.56,
     "text": "She was the Uncrowned."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 10,
   "title": "Which Memory Will Answer?",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_10.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 473590,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_10.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 280261,
   "duration": 31.01,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 9.79,
     "text": "Inside, the Echoes rose against her. And when they fell, they released the resonance trapped within them… and her blood could gather it."
    },
    {
     "t0": 10.54,
     "t1": 16.5,
     "text": "With that power, she could force the castle to choose… and another memory would answer."
    },
    {
     "t0": 17.25,
     "t1": 23.49,
     "text": "Rubble gathered itself back into walls. Torches burned where only moonlight had been."
    },
    {
     "t0": 24.24,
     "t1": 26.44,
     "text": "She did not travel through history."
    },
    {
     "t0": 27.54,
     "t1": 30.23,
     "text": "The castle changed… around her."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 11,
   "title": "What the Stones Confessed",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_11.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 436700,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_11.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 256758,
   "duration": 28.01,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 3.24,
     "text": "But the castle's two memories did not agree."
    },
    {
     "t0": 3.99,
     "t1": 11.69,
     "text": "A door that stood sealed in the Past… lay broken outward in the Present. The wounds were in the wrong places."
    },
    {
     "t0": 12.44,
     "t1": 18.71,
     "text": "The stones told a different history. The people of Caer Veyr had not been defending their king."
    },
    {
     "t0": 19.46,
     "t1": 21.48,
     "text": "They had been trying to escape him."
    },
    {
     "t0": 22.58,
     "t1": 27.23,
     "text": "The siege was real. But the catastrophe… was Aldren's."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 12,
   "title": "The Last Crown",
   "image": "assets/lore/page_12.webp",
   "width": 1024,
   "height": 1536,
   "imageBytes": 473536,
   "placeholder": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
   "audio": "assets/lore/narration_12.ogg",
   "audioBytes": 283990,
   "duration": 31.41,
   "cues": [
    {
     "t0": 0.28,
     "t1": 11.34,
     "text": "Aldren did not die in the Sundering. He remained… fused with the Crownheart, until king, castle and memory could no longer be told apart."
    },
    {
     "t0": 12.09,
     "t1": 13.45,
     "text": "The Last Crown."
    },
    {
     "t0": 14.2,
     "t1": 20.92,
     "text": "He still believes Veyr can be saved. And her unbound blood… might finish his ritual."
    },
    {
     "t0": 21.67,
     "t1": 24.98,
     "text": "She had come to claim her inheritance."
    },
    {
     "t0": 25.73,
     "t1": 27.25,
     "text": "Now she had to ask…"
    },
    {
     "t0": 28.35,
     "t1": 30.64,
     "text": "should this inheritance survive at all?"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
